- **Repetition.** The same trick, "one row/column fills exactly, then chain", is the opening note in about half the levels. The exact-fit colour rows in L25-L36 and the "read the hidden line from its crossings" smudge levels in L73-L84 sound alike. Several breathers (L7, L19, L31, L43) reuse an earlier fill-notch board instead of a new shape idea.
- **Chapters with weak ideas.** Stamp is the thinnest. L51 and L52 repeat L50, and L70's stamp is nearly decorative. Observatory's "deep-chain" is a label rather than a distinct mechanic, so L97 teaches nothing new.
- **Data fault.** L82 is labelled "smudged row 8" but its text says row 7. Fix this before launch.
- **Pacing.** L99 is billed as gentle but plays at 63% casual between two harder boards. Kiln and Lantern sit in the mid-50s from the middle of each chapter, which is on target but leaves few real breathers. Late-game small boards (L110-L112, L115) are under-sized for their place.
- **Fairness.** I can't see a guess-forced level, and trap rate is 0 everywhere.
